  number={},
  pages={511-516},
  abstract={The issue of energy waste in commercial and learning facilities attracts significant attention as the traditional HVAC and light systems are usually programmed following the clock or operated manually without focusing on the real time occupancy. This causes poor energy consumption and high expenses of operation. To overcome this issue, we suggest an occupancy-based energy-saving system that combines the IoT sensors with deep learning models to predictive control. The system will use several sensors (PIR, CO2 and thermal sensor) connected to an ESP32 microcontroller to detect real time occupancy. A deep learning model is implemented as a cloudhosted solution and predicts occupancy patterns of rooms and dynamically controls HVAC and lighting systems by using relay-based actuation. Also, there is an admin dashboard with monitoring, manual override, and energy usage analytics. The experimental analysis shows that the potential of energy consumption reduction and occupant comfort are very high. The suggested system is an affordable, scalable, and solution to the sustainable and intelligent building energy management.},
