  abstract={As smart building technology evolves, balancing automated control and user privacy has become a critical challenge. This study proposes an architecture that integrates edge computing directly into the perception layer for environmental monitoring and occupancy sensing. By utilizing a 60GHz frequency modulated continuous wave radar instead of traditional cameras and performing localized computation on a microcontroller unit-based edge node, the system ensures visual privacy and data sovereignty. The proof of concept demonstrates that shifting intelligence to the sensing domain effectively minimizes data exposure while maintaining real-time responsiveness without reliance on external cloud services.},
